From 69ad192cf9276c510dae41f2d41606c63cdd5429 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leonieziechmann <48921293+leonieziechmann@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:29:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] refactor(data): name the namespace `data`, after the
 parameter it feeds

The maintainer's decision on Q19: canonical names, single descriptive
words where possible. The root namespace `invoice-data` becomes `data`,
the house rule for a namespace that feeds a parameter (`theme:`/`theme`,
`locale:`/`locale`): `invoice(data: data.load(..))`. Its file
src/public/invoice-data.typ becomes src/public/data.typ.

The string constants `input-key` and `file-key` leave the public
namespace (8 names: format, load, decode, check, values, party, items,
schema); they stay internal in contract/input.typ, and the doc comment of
`load` names the two --input keys.

A file that binds `data` itself (`#let data = json(..)` after the
package import) hides the namespace; `invoice(data: <dictionary>)` still
works, and the docs name the record `record`. The messages (`data:
data.load(read: ..)`, `data.items[..]`), the comments, the export pin and
the contract tests follow; the marker's internal frame kind is
`data-items`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RaaQussN1QVEE8zRWeeCD3
